cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "LUMA WNBA Stint and ARC Corpus"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-16"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://github.com/lumahoops/WNBA"
repository-code: "https://github.com/lumahoops/WNBA"
abstract: >
  Lineup-stint corpus for the Women's National Basketball Association. A stint is a segment
  of game time during which the ten players on court do not change. The corpus contains 267,293
  stints across 24 regular seasons (2003-2026) and 23 postseasons (2003-2025), covering 5,623
  games, current through 2026-08-15. Reconstructed from play-by-play substitution events;
  each record gives both five-player lineups, duration in seconds, points scored by each team,
  and a sixteen-element event tally per team. 974 players are identified by persistent
  identifiers with a crosswalk to WNBA Stats and ESPN source identifiers. Validated against
  independently sourced box scores; per-season reconstruction diagnostics are distributed
  with the data.
